    "result_text": "The people sheet now has a \"Fathom mean\" row, and the acceptance test passes when run with `bin/e2e`.\n\nThe row is `data-testid=\"rollup-fathom-mean\"` and sits right after \"Fathom even\" in the table footer. I added it in `src/main/frontend/src/app/features/people/people-list.ts` as `fathomMean`. It works like the existing Fathom low and Fathom top rows:\n\n- **Who counts:** people on hold are left out, and so are people whose fathom is n/a.\n- **Rounding:** the sum is divided by the count with the sheet's shared `divide()` helper, so it rounds to the nearest whole number with halves rounding up, the same as every other divide.\n- **Nobody counted:** if no one qualifies, the row shows `n/a`.\n\nOnly the front end changed. Fathom is already worked out on the server for each person, so the server, database and test-data endpoints didn't need to change.",
